1
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:42,840
Don't you think Nada
cares too much about that kid?

2
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:44,840
The kid whose name sounds like Rawich's?

3
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:46,480
Their names really do sound alike.

4
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:48,760
This is getting interesting.

5
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:51,440
Grandpa went with your idea, Wee.

6
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:53,000
<i>He decided to hold a press conference.</i>

7
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:54,880
<i>One voice won over three.</i>

8
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:57,320
<i>Looks like he really values your opinion.</i>

9
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:59,440
Maybe this place suits you more than me.

10
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:03,440
Alyssa said
the response was very positive,

11
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:05,880
so I told her it was your work.

12
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:06,880
Thank you very much.

13
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:15,200
This is my hat.

14
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:17,920
I was waiting for you
to return my hair tie.

15
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:37,840
Mom.

16
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:41,680
What is it?

17
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:45,320
May I take the MD to the event with me?

18
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:47,520
Sure.

19
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:48,600
Let's go.

20
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:07,320
Rawee, what are you doing here?

21
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:09,920
He's driving us today,

22
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:11,960
so he can come along too.

23
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:16,040
Well, let's go, then.

24
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:01,840
Dad!

25
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:18,920
Someone's getting protective
of his daughter.

26
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:22,000
I come by all the time.

27
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:25,160
Have a seat.

28
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:33,680
So, are you two dating?

29
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:36,560
See? I knew it.

30
00:05:38,520 --> 00:05:41,600
Have you met Phakorn before?

31
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:43,720
Just once.

32
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:45,320
Before he went to America.

33
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:50,400
I hope he's nothing
like his older brother.

34
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:52,880
I can't stand that one.

35
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:55,400
And you never said a word

36
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:57,240
about letting him rent the house.

37
00:05:57,320 --> 00:05:59,480
Oh, I forgot to tell you.

38
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:01,200
Rawee's dependable.

39
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:04,720
He works hard,
and he can help you two out.

40
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:06,520
It's just the two of you here.

41
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:07,720
I worry.

42
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:10,880
He seems serious to me too.

43
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:13,200
He's straightforward, like me.

44
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:15,200
You two are nothing alike.

45
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,600
Anyway, what's the younger brother like?

46
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:23,680
Thamrong knows that family.
You'd have to ask him.

47
00:06:23,760 --> 00:06:25,640
But I do know

48
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:27,920
Phakorn did very well in school.

49
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:32,880
Billionaire genes, huh?

50
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:39,200
I'll get us some cold drinks.

51
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:45,840
I'll have to call your Aunt Da
and have a word with her.

52
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:48,360
Her son's dating my daughter,

53
00:06:48,440 --> 00:06:49,680
and she didn't even tell me.

54
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:07,320
Mom.

55
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:09,920
I'd like to bring a friend in
to help me at work.

56
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,520
He's good.
I think he could really help me.

57
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:14,760
Is he trustworthy?

58
00:07:14,840 --> 00:07:17,440
I've known him since I was in America.

59
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:18,920
Four or five years now.

60
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:22,240
Bring him by so I can meet him first.

61
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:23,920
Sure.

62
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:28,640
Rawee.

63
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:29,760
Thank you

64
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:32,120
for staying late to help me every day.

65
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:35,400
I just had some work to finish.

66
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:38,640
You barely had any work left.

67
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:42,480
I know what Taddao assigned you.

68
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:44,720
Thank you.

69
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:45,760
Yes.

70
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:49,520
That's just how Rawee is, Mom.

71
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:51,680
When I was sick as a kid,

72
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:53,960
he'd stay up all night looking after me.

73
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:19,600
Mom, want a coffee? I can go get you one.

74
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:20,760
It's okay.

75
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:22,960
I'll get a snack too.

76
00:08:23,040 --> 00:08:25,120
Do either of you want a coffee?

77
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:28,960
No, thanks. I've already had mine.

78
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,360
I've had two cups already.

79
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:33,080
I had a late night.

80
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:35,559
Where did you go? When did you get home?

81
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,280
I went out for dinner,

82
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:40,799
then listened to some music
with Alyssa for a bit.

83
00:08:44,159 --> 00:08:45,560
Just a bit?

84
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:47,040
I can smell the alcohol on you.

85
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:48,760
It's only once in a while.

86
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:50,800
I hope so.

87
00:08:50,880 --> 00:08:53,080
You know you're not
as healthy as everyone else.

88
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:54,320
Don't drink too much, okay?

89
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:56,240
Okay.

90
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:12,920
Wee.

91
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,960
What do you think of Alyssa?

92
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:18,160
Why do you ask?

93
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:21,720
I just want to know

94
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:23,280
what you think

95
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:24,840
of her.

96
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:30,280
I don't know. I don't know her that well.

97
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:33,440
Really?

98
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:35,560
I thought you did.

99
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:37,520
I saw you two leave together last night.

100
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:13,200
Is something wrong
between you and your brother?

101
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:18,840
If you want to talk to Korn, let me know.

102
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:20,440
I can call him.

103
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:24,600
It's okay. I'll see him tomorrow anyway.

104
00:10:29,040 --> 00:10:30,240
How are you getting home?

105
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:33,240
Want a ride? It's on my way.

106
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:36,200
It's okay. I can get home on my own.

107
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:41,040
If Korn found out I ran into his brother

108
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:43,920
and let him go home alone
when we live so close,

109
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,600
he wouldn't be happy.

110
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:49,160
Then don't tell him.

111
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:54,080
Come with me.

112
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:57,680
It's late. Getting a ride might be hard.

113
00:10:57,760 --> 00:11:01,080
Don't you have to get up early
to go out of town tomorrow?

114
00:11:58,480 --> 00:12:00,000
She was just being kind.

115
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:02,240
Don't read too much into it.

116
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:06,160
I didn't think anything of it.

117
00:12:06,240 --> 00:12:08,680
I know Alyssa is kind

118
00:12:08,760 --> 00:12:10,760
and down-to-earth.

119
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:14,080
I'm more worried about you.

120
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:18,200
I don't feel that way about her, Korn.

121
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:21,000
I trust you, Wee.

122
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:46,080
Where did you get this hat?

123
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:49,200
It's Korn's.

124
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:51,880
He lent it to me when we first met
because it was raining.

125
00:12:56,040 --> 00:12:58,640
My mom says you'll get sick

126
00:12:58,720 --> 00:13:00,040
if your head gets wet.

127
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:52,440
Alright, I'm ready. Let's go.

128
00:13:57,640 --> 00:13:59,080
Mom!

129
00:14:05,560 --> 00:14:08,440
Yes, okay. Thank you.

130
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:13,360
Nimit!

131
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:16,800
Nada got shot.

132
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:20,120
-You're kidding.
-It's true.

133
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:22,320
My friend just called.
Her husband's a cop.

134
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:25,080
How's Aunt Da?

135
00:14:25,160 --> 00:14:27,520
They're taking her to the hospital now.

136
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:34,760
Father!

137
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:35,880
Father!

138
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:37,800
Da's been shot!

139
00:14:38,840 --> 00:14:39,800
What did you say?

140
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:41,200
Da's been shot.

141
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:44,960
What is it, Panas?

142
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:48,440
What's all the shouting?
Tell us what happened.

143
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:49,800
Da's been shot.

144
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:52,520
Get the car.

145
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:54,840
Father, where are you going?

146
00:14:54,920 --> 00:14:57,640
-Get the car!
-Father, where are you going?

147
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:58,880
To see Da.

148
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:01,640
Calm down. Start again.

149
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:03,640
Where did it happen? Tell us everything.

150
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:07,200
According to the news,
she's in the hospital now.

151
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:08,640
Is she dead?

152
00:15:08,720 --> 00:15:09,800
Pim.

153
00:15:12,560 --> 00:15:15,120
Father, you don't need to go.

154
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:16,880
I'll go check on her.

155
00:15:25,040 --> 00:15:26,120
Father.

156
00:15:26,840 --> 00:15:28,360
We can't trust Pim with this.

157
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:30,080
Then you go too.

158
00:15:30,160 --> 00:15:32,360
If anything happens,
report directly to me.

159
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:33,480
Understood?

160
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:36,320
Yes, Father. I'll look after Da.

161
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:37,440
Good.

162
00:15:58,680 --> 00:15:59,920
Oh, Uncle Thamrong.

163
00:16:01,280 --> 00:16:02,400
How did you hear about it so soon?

164
00:16:02,480 --> 00:16:05,320
I was nearby. As soon as I heard,
I came straight here.

165
00:16:05,400 --> 00:16:07,280
Do you know how Da got shot?

166
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:09,160
I heard they mistook her
for someone else, Sir.

167
00:16:12,320 --> 00:16:14,520
THONBURI BAMRUNGMUANG HOSPITAL

168
00:16:22,760 --> 00:16:23,760
Pimpa.

169
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:25,280
Oh, Aoy.

170
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:27,240
-How are you? Good to see you.
-Hello.

171
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:30,600
I heard you're the head nurse now.
Is that right?

172
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:32,840
-Yes.
-Have you been well?

173
00:16:32,920 --> 00:16:34,160
I have.

174
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:36,320
How about you, Pim?

175
00:16:36,400 --> 00:16:37,760
I've been well.

176
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:41,320
I'm here to see someone
from the family. She was shot.

177
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:44,960
Is it Ms. Nada?

178
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:49,080
Um… well, yes.

179
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:52,000
She's in surgery now.

180
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:53,600
-Is she?
-Yes.

181
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:56,480
Oh, Mim.

182
00:16:57,560 --> 00:17:00,240
Could you take these documents
to the VIP room for me?

183
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:01,520
-Sure.
-Thanks.

184
00:17:02,440 --> 00:17:04,119
This way, please.

185
00:17:04,200 --> 00:17:05,440
Alright.

186
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:13,079
-Phakorn. Oh, hey.
-Hello.

187
00:17:13,960 --> 00:17:15,200
Are you two alright?

188
00:17:15,280 --> 00:17:17,040
We're fine.

189
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:18,839
You're lucky

190
00:17:18,920 --> 00:17:20,720
neither of you got hit.

191
00:17:22,599 --> 00:17:24,240
Have the police questioned you yet?

192
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:26,200
Yes, they have.

193
00:17:29,400 --> 00:17:30,760
Did you see the shooter's face?

194
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:33,440
I didn't.

195
00:17:33,520 --> 00:17:35,200
He was wearing a helmet.

196
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:38,000
I saw him following us from the house.

197
00:17:38,680 --> 00:17:40,520
I thought it was strange,
but I never imagined--

198
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:42,640
Then Aunt Da wasn't shot by mistake,

199
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:44,800
like you'd heard, Uncle Thamrong.

200
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:49,440
Or maybe someone made up that story
to confuse everyone.

201
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:51,880
I'll go talk to the police.

202
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:53,080
Okay.

203
00:17:59,280 --> 00:18:01,560
Excuse me. Are you Ms. Nada's family?

204
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:03,160
Yes.

205
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:07,000
She's lost a lot of blood.
We need extra blood on hand.

206
00:18:07,760 --> 00:18:09,600
Does anyone share Ms. Nada's blood type?

207
00:18:09,680 --> 00:18:10,800
Rawee does.

208
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:15,440
So do I.

209
00:18:17,440 --> 00:18:19,280
Please come with me.

210
00:18:32,760 --> 00:18:34,080
Uncle, how did you know

211
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:36,720
Mr. Rawee's blood type matches Aunt Da's?

212
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:38,880
Well…

213
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:41,400
I've known this family for a long time.

214
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:44,960
They're all type O.
They've donated blood at the factory.

215
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:48,880
Even though Phakorn is adopted,

216
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:49,920
he has the same blood type?

217
00:18:51,160 --> 00:18:52,120
Yes.

218
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:54,400
That's why I never knew

219
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:56,360
this family had adopted a child.

220
00:18:56,440 --> 00:18:59,520
But you know now

221
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:01,520
that Phakorn is Aunt Da's son.

222
00:19:01,600 --> 00:19:03,760
But when the nurse asked for blood,

223
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:07,400
you named Mr. Rawee first.

224
00:19:09,440 --> 00:19:12,160
You're quite curious, Ms. Alyssa.

225
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:15,000
I just know Rawee better.

226
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:35,320
So who is that boy?

227
00:19:35,400 --> 00:19:38,040
His name's Rawee. Do you know him?

228
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:40,440
Rawee?

229
00:19:44,520 --> 00:19:46,560
He works for Nada.

230
00:19:48,560 --> 00:19:51,480
From what I heard,
they seem to be brothers.

231
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:06,840
I'd like to have Rawee,
my new assistant, join the meeting.

232
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:08,760
He'll need to be involved anyway.

233
00:20:08,840 --> 00:20:10,280
New assistant?

234
00:20:10,360 --> 00:20:11,560
Yes.

235
00:20:11,640 --> 00:20:13,000
-Rawee?
-Yes.

236
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:15,920
He's the older brother
who grew up with Phakorn.

237
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,680
He's currently helping Phakorn.

238
00:20:23,040 --> 00:20:26,440
Don't you think Nada
cares too much about that kid?

239
00:20:26,520 --> 00:20:27,640
What kid?

240
00:20:27,720 --> 00:20:31,120
The kid who grew up
in the same house as Phakorn.

241
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:33,440
The kid whose name sounds like Rawich's?

242
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:38,520
But seriously,
he kind of looks like him too.

243
00:20:39,320 --> 00:20:40,680
Don't tell me that kid is…

244
00:20:41,280 --> 00:20:42,440
Isn't it true?

245
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:44,720
This is getting interesting.

246
00:20:48,200 --> 00:20:49,800
I need the DNA test results.

247
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:51,640
Please help me.

248
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:55,000
For Ms. Nada and Mr. Phakorn?

249
00:20:55,080 --> 00:20:56,920
Rawee's too.

250
00:21:00,840 --> 00:21:04,600
I know it's a serious breach of ethics,

251
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:06,360
but I need to know.

252
00:21:10,040 --> 00:21:11,120
Just think about it.

253
00:21:11,800 --> 00:21:13,960
What if that boy isn't really my nephew?

254
00:21:14,680 --> 00:21:16,440
Imagine the shame if our family

255
00:21:16,520 --> 00:21:19,960
gave a share of the inheritance
to some nobody.

256
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:23,360
I've been suspicious for a long time

257
00:21:24,080 --> 00:21:27,520
about why Nada refuses to take a DNA test

258
00:21:27,600 --> 00:21:30,360
and officially acknowledge
Phakorn as her son.

259
00:21:31,120 --> 00:21:33,680
She must be hiding something.

260
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:43,120
I won't tell anyone.

261
00:21:45,160 --> 00:21:46,240
How about this?

262
00:21:48,080 --> 00:21:50,360
I'll give you something for your trouble.

263
00:21:51,320 --> 00:21:53,560
For the risk you're taking.

264
00:21:55,360 --> 00:21:56,680
Please help me.

265
00:22:27,800 --> 00:22:28,920
Ms. Nada is safe now.

266
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:30,400
The surgery went well.

267
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:32,680
What a relief.

268
00:22:33,280 --> 00:22:34,640
-Thank you, Doctor.
-Thank you.

269
00:22:34,720 --> 00:22:35,560
-Thank you.
-Sure.

270
00:22:35,640 --> 00:22:36,600
You're welcome.

271
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:41,520
She hasn't regained consciousness yet.
You can visit her tomorrow.

272
00:22:41,600 --> 00:22:42,560
Alright.

273
00:22:46,640 --> 00:22:48,240
So there's nothing to worry about now.

274
00:22:50,080 --> 00:22:53,040
She was lucky
the bullet missed her vital organs.

275
00:22:57,240 --> 00:23:00,280
We can head home, then.

276
00:23:00,360 --> 00:23:02,160
-Come on.
-Good.

277
00:23:02,920 --> 00:23:04,800
I thought her injuries would be worse.

278
00:23:05,480 --> 00:23:06,640
I'm off, then.

279
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:12,440
I'll head off now.

280
00:23:13,280 --> 00:23:14,840
Goodbye.

281
00:23:21,280 --> 00:23:22,240
Take care, okay?

282
00:23:23,400 --> 00:23:24,600
I'll take you home.

283
00:23:25,200 --> 00:23:28,920
It's alright. I'll take her.
Stay here with Wee.

284
00:23:32,040 --> 00:23:32,920
Let's go, Ms. Alyssa.

285
00:23:36,160 --> 00:23:37,320
I'll call you later.

286
00:23:51,080 --> 00:23:52,480
See, Wee?

287
00:23:53,320 --> 00:23:55,840
Mr. Thamrong is acting strange.

288
00:24:00,080 --> 00:24:01,600
I didn't notice anything, Korn.

289
00:24:02,520 --> 00:24:03,680
Don't overthink it.

290
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:07,280
Go home and get some rest.

291
00:24:08,280 --> 00:24:09,960
I'll stay here for now.

292
00:24:13,720 --> 00:24:16,240
Then I'll come back and take over later.

293
00:24:40,440 --> 00:24:43,120
Father, Da's out of danger now.

294
00:24:44,040 --> 00:24:46,200
Pim already called to tell me.

295
00:24:47,680 --> 00:24:49,480
Why didn't you stay there?

296
00:24:51,800 --> 00:24:54,640
Well, there were plenty
of people with her,

297
00:24:55,360 --> 00:24:57,040
so I came back to look after you.

298
00:24:57,800 --> 00:25:00,400
I was worried you'd be so concerned
about Da that you wouldn't eat.

299
00:25:01,960 --> 00:25:03,560
She's out of danger.

300
00:25:04,160 --> 00:25:06,000
There's probably nothing
to worry about now.

301
00:25:12,880 --> 00:25:13,920
Father.

302
00:25:14,680 --> 00:25:16,880
Who will you send in her place

303
00:25:17,800 --> 00:25:19,640
to the project's closing party?

304
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:24,120
I've already taken care of it.
Don't worry.

305
00:25:29,840 --> 00:25:31,080
Yes, Father.

306
00:25:34,920 --> 00:25:38,280
Ms. Nada's out of danger, Mom.
She's in the ICU.

307
00:25:40,120 --> 00:25:42,160
I'll call you again tomorrow.

308
00:25:52,400 --> 00:25:53,600
<i>Who are you driving for?</i>

309
00:25:54,680 --> 00:25:57,080
Mr. Panas. You know him?

310
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:58,920
He's my boss's younger brother.

311
00:26:00,520 --> 00:26:01,760
Who's your boss?

312
00:26:02,360 --> 00:26:03,360
Ms. Nada.

313
00:26:03,440 --> 00:26:06,120
Hey, Wee.

314
00:26:06,680 --> 00:26:08,320
I'm warning you.

315
00:26:09,040 --> 00:26:10,800
Stay away from Ms. Nada.

316
00:26:21,760 --> 00:26:24,960
Taddao, I need a favor.

317
00:26:27,200 --> 00:26:30,640
An old friend of mine works here.
Could you get me his number?

318
00:26:32,920 --> 00:26:36,360
His name's Kongphob.
He drives for Mr. Panas.

319
00:26:52,840 --> 00:26:56,040
You seem more worried
about Nada than her own son is.

320
00:26:58,600 --> 00:27:00,640
Ms. Pimpa, you're still here?

321
00:27:06,760 --> 00:27:09,800
I came to take over from Phakorn.

322
00:27:09,880 --> 00:27:11,880
He went home to get some clothes.

323
00:27:11,960 --> 00:27:13,360
I'm sure he'll be back soon.

324
00:27:15,320 --> 00:27:16,600
You two seem close.

325
00:27:17,800 --> 00:27:21,000
I only just found out
you grew up together.

326
00:27:24,640 --> 00:27:26,280
But you know,

327
00:27:26,360 --> 00:27:28,520
I think you look

328
00:27:28,600 --> 00:27:31,280
more like Nada and Rawich
than Phakorn does.

329
00:27:35,280 --> 00:27:38,600
What do you mean, Ms. Pimpa?
I don't understand.

330
00:27:41,880 --> 00:27:44,520
You really are slow to catch on.

331
00:27:58,360 --> 00:28:00,920
I just hope history doesn't repeat itself.

332
00:28:02,680 --> 00:28:04,080
Do you think

333
00:28:04,160 --> 00:28:06,840
the people who hurt Aunt Da
are the same ones as before?

334
00:28:08,240 --> 00:28:09,840
She's never had enemies.

335
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:14,120
The only people who'd want her dead

336
00:28:14,200 --> 00:28:16,240
are those who stand to lose out.

337
00:28:18,800 --> 00:28:21,320
Why would they act now?

338
00:28:21,400 --> 00:28:24,480
Well, she's running Tayawat Group now.

339
00:28:25,120 --> 00:28:29,000
And she's found the family's
only grandson. Who wouldn't be jealous?

340
00:28:32,520 --> 00:28:35,520
You're close to Phakorn, so be careful.

341
00:28:36,120 --> 00:28:37,720
You could get hurt too.

342
00:28:38,560 --> 00:28:39,840
I will, Dad.

343
00:28:52,760 --> 00:28:56,040
You look awfully happy
since your sister got shot.

344
00:29:00,120 --> 00:29:02,440
You're the one who seems happy.

345
00:29:03,560 --> 00:29:04,840
What's that supposed to mean?

346
00:29:06,160 --> 00:29:08,880
You volunteered
to look after Da for Father.

347
00:29:08,960 --> 00:29:10,400
Why?

348
00:29:10,480 --> 00:29:12,240
Were you worried she might survive

349
00:29:12,320 --> 00:29:14,200
and you'd inherit less?

350
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:17,880
It was you, right?

351
00:29:17,960 --> 00:29:19,160
What?

352
00:29:19,760 --> 00:29:22,400
You hired someone to shoot her,
didn't you?

353
00:29:23,400 --> 00:29:24,560
Why would I do that?

354
00:29:25,080 --> 00:29:26,320
More likely, it was you.

355
00:29:27,480 --> 00:29:29,800
Me? Why would I?

356
00:29:31,400 --> 00:29:33,400
Maybe you're angry

357
00:29:33,480 --> 00:29:35,360
she removed you from the company board.

358
00:29:36,320 --> 00:29:37,640
What have you heard?

359
00:29:39,480 --> 00:29:41,560
What have you heard?

360
00:29:41,640 --> 00:29:43,600
-Tell me what you know!
-Let go of me first.

361
00:29:47,600 --> 00:29:49,280
That news about the fortune teller,

362
00:29:49,880 --> 00:29:51,880
didn't Da leak it

363
00:29:51,960 --> 00:29:53,280
to get back at you

364
00:29:54,040 --> 00:29:56,480
for accusing her of hiding company shares?

365
00:29:58,400 --> 00:30:00,000
That bitch, Nada.

366
00:30:00,600 --> 00:30:01,560
What?

367
00:30:01,640 --> 00:30:03,560
Now you wish the shooter had killed her?

368
00:30:04,200 --> 00:30:07,440
Hey. If I'd hired someone to shoot her,

369
00:30:07,520 --> 00:30:10,080
she'd be dead.
I wouldn't have let them miss.

370
00:30:10,680 --> 00:30:13,120
You hired the shooter,

371
00:30:13,200 --> 00:30:15,640
and now you're trying to pin it on me.

372
00:30:15,720 --> 00:30:17,320
Nonsense.

373
00:30:17,400 --> 00:30:19,440
I'm not after the inheritance
like you are.

374
00:30:21,240 --> 00:30:23,800
Maybe you are. Who knows?

375
00:30:27,040 --> 00:30:28,200
By the way,

376
00:30:28,840 --> 00:30:31,880
do you know anything
about Phakorn's original family?

377
00:30:32,920 --> 00:30:36,720
No. I've never been interested. Why?

378
00:30:37,440 --> 00:30:39,720
Just a thought.

379
00:30:39,800 --> 00:30:43,280
If that family really did con Nada,

380
00:30:43,360 --> 00:30:45,320
imagine how flustered they'd get

381
00:30:45,400 --> 00:30:47,440
if they had to face her.

382
00:31:23,320 --> 00:31:25,400
-Hello?
-Korn.

383
00:31:26,160 --> 00:31:27,240
Where are you?

384
00:31:28,480 --> 00:31:29,800
Who is this?

385
00:31:29,880 --> 00:31:31,440
It's Wee.

386
00:31:32,400 --> 00:31:33,480
Are you still asleep?

387
00:31:34,600 --> 00:31:37,640
I called to tell you
Ms. Nada's doing better.

388
00:31:37,720 --> 00:31:39,160
She'll be out of the ICU soon.

389
00:31:43,720 --> 00:31:45,320
Okay. I'll be right there.

390
00:31:46,080 --> 00:31:49,440
INTENSIVE CARE UNIT

391
00:32:21,920 --> 00:32:24,040
Does anyone share Ms. Nada's blood type?

392
00:32:24,120 --> 00:32:25,240
Rawee does.

393
00:32:28,800 --> 00:32:29,880
So do I.

394
00:32:31,240 --> 00:32:33,560
How did Uncle Thamrong
know Wee's blood type?

395
00:32:35,080 --> 00:32:36,360
Are they close?

396
00:32:56,080 --> 00:32:58,440
Where are you going? You look lovely.

397
00:32:59,120 --> 00:33:01,080
I told you yesterday.

398
00:33:01,160 --> 00:33:03,120
I'm going out to eat with Pimpa.

399
00:33:03,840 --> 00:33:05,600
Phakorn's aunt.

400
00:33:07,320 --> 00:33:10,040
I've been suspicious for a long time

401
00:33:10,120 --> 00:33:11,840
about why Nada

402
00:33:11,920 --> 00:33:13,560
refuses to take a DNA test

403
00:33:13,640 --> 00:33:16,600
and officially acknowledge
Phakorn as her son.

404
00:33:17,240 --> 00:33:19,720
She must be hiding something.

405
00:33:21,240 --> 00:33:22,320
Can I come too?

406
00:33:25,160 --> 00:33:27,880
Want to get to know
your boyfriend's family?

407
00:33:28,680 --> 00:33:31,440
Oops, I mean your friend's family.

408
00:33:32,880 --> 00:33:35,000
It'd be good to get to know them,
wouldn't it?

409
00:33:35,080 --> 00:33:36,040
Yes.

410
00:33:36,120 --> 00:33:37,840
It'd be very good, dear.

411
00:33:37,920 --> 00:33:41,200
Pim will be thrilled when she hears.

412
00:33:41,280 --> 00:33:43,600
She's been looking for allies.

413
00:33:44,320 --> 00:33:46,360
I'll go get dressed, then.

414
00:33:46,440 --> 00:33:49,600
Go ahead. Take your time.
We've still got a while.

415
00:33:49,680 --> 00:33:51,080
-I'll let her know.
-Okay.

416
00:34:06,280 --> 00:34:07,680
Could you wait a moment?

417
00:34:09,960 --> 00:34:12,520
<i>Your friend didn't leave a phone number.</i>

418
00:34:12,600 --> 00:34:15,280
<i>He lost his phone</i>
<i>and said he'd give us his number later.</i>

419
00:34:15,840 --> 00:34:17,560
<i>I only have his home address.</i>

420
00:34:32,280 --> 00:34:35,239
This is Mrs. Walai,
from the family Phakorn grew up with.

421
00:34:37,400 --> 00:34:39,239
-Hello.
-Hello.

422
00:34:42,320 --> 00:34:46,239
You do look a bit like Phakorn,
Mrs. Walai.

423
00:34:48,679 --> 00:34:51,199
You're the only one who says that.

424
00:34:51,280 --> 00:34:54,880
Most people say the three of us

425
00:34:54,960 --> 00:34:56,520
don't look alike at all.

426
00:34:59,400 --> 00:35:02,080
Thank you for taking care of Phakorn.

427
00:35:02,880 --> 00:35:04,600
It must have been hard on you.

428
00:35:05,880 --> 00:35:07,200
Not at all, Sir.

429
00:35:07,280 --> 00:35:10,760
Phakorn was a good boy.
He was bright and easy to raise.

430
00:35:10,840 --> 00:35:13,320
He never gave us any trouble.

431
00:35:14,120 --> 00:35:16,560
If you ever need anything, let me know.

432
00:35:16,640 --> 00:35:18,120
Don't hesitate.

433
00:35:19,160 --> 00:35:20,520
Thank you, Sir.

434
00:35:21,840 --> 00:35:24,640
I hear your son works for us too.

435
00:35:25,400 --> 00:35:26,840
Yes, he does.

436
00:35:26,920 --> 00:35:29,000
Well, that's good.

437
00:35:32,120 --> 00:35:36,240
Where's Nada's only son, anyway?

438
00:35:36,880 --> 00:35:39,040
Everyone else has come to see his mother,

439
00:35:39,640 --> 00:35:40,960
but there's no sign of him.

440
00:35:44,080 --> 00:35:45,880
Why are you meddling in their business?

441
00:35:47,200 --> 00:35:50,000
I just thought we could all meet at once.
The old mother

442
00:35:50,080 --> 00:35:52,520
and the new mother, Father.

443
00:36:07,120 --> 00:36:09,920
We'll move Ms. Nada to room 1140 shortly.

444
00:36:13,480 --> 00:36:15,160
Let's wait for Da in her room.

445
00:36:16,160 --> 00:36:17,000
Are you coming,

446
00:36:17,920 --> 00:36:19,280
or do you have lunch plans?

447
00:36:35,520 --> 00:36:38,160
Hey, let me be blunt.

448
00:36:38,240 --> 00:36:40,200
Don't say I'm gossiping.

449
00:36:40,280 --> 00:36:42,120
The truth is the truth.

450
00:36:44,800 --> 00:36:46,000
Nada's mother

451
00:36:46,720 --> 00:36:48,120
was a maid in our house.

452
00:36:48,200 --> 00:36:49,280
Huh?

453
00:36:51,200 --> 00:36:52,520
Oh my God.

454
00:36:55,920 --> 00:37:00,440
See? That's why I hate her so much.

455
00:37:00,520 --> 00:37:03,480
You never told me that.

456
00:37:03,560 --> 00:37:04,920
I thought

457
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:08,600
you siblings were jealous of her
because she was Mr. Prachak's favorite.

458
00:37:09,200 --> 00:37:10,280
Hey.

459
00:37:10,960 --> 00:37:13,280
Who'd want to tell people
that their father

460
00:37:13,360 --> 00:37:16,080
took the maid as his wife?

461
00:37:18,320 --> 00:37:22,880
Well, I saw that you're seeing Phakorn.

462
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:26,760
You'd find out sooner or later,

463
00:37:26,840 --> 00:37:29,480
so I wanted to tell you first.

464
00:37:32,080 --> 00:37:34,520
Come to think of it,

465
00:37:34,600 --> 00:37:36,640
she's lucky, isn't she?

466
00:37:36,720 --> 00:37:39,440
She's been attacked twice

467
00:37:39,520 --> 00:37:41,320
and survived both times.

468
00:37:41,920 --> 00:37:43,320
And the rest of us suffer for it.

469
00:37:44,240 --> 00:37:47,200
The police keep calling us in
for questioning.

470
00:37:49,640 --> 00:37:51,120
But now that she's survived,

471
00:37:51,760 --> 00:37:55,920
I hope the old Nada finally comes back.

472
00:37:59,000 --> 00:38:00,280
What do you mean?

473
00:38:01,560 --> 00:38:03,280
The last time she fell and hit her head,

474
00:38:03,360 --> 00:38:05,480
she lost her memory.

475
00:38:05,560 --> 00:38:08,200
When she woke up,
she was a real piece of work.

476
00:38:08,280 --> 00:38:10,640
She used to be so meek.

477
00:38:10,720 --> 00:38:12,720
She's been fighting us ever since.

478
00:38:13,840 --> 00:38:16,000
She had a head injury.

479
00:38:17,000 --> 00:38:19,440
She might as well have been possessed.

480
00:38:20,800 --> 00:38:22,160
Let's hope whatever got into her

481
00:38:22,240 --> 00:38:23,920
is gone when she wakes up.

482
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:26,040
Then she'll be easier to control.

483
00:38:35,400 --> 00:38:38,160
-Wee.
-What is it?

484
00:38:42,640 --> 00:38:45,160
Well, I'm sorry

485
00:38:45,240 --> 00:38:47,080
I was so cold to you.

486
00:38:48,120 --> 00:38:49,600
What are you apologizing for?

487
00:38:50,280 --> 00:38:52,040
I was in the wrong.

488
00:38:53,080 --> 00:38:54,840
You had every right to sulk.

489
00:38:56,240 --> 00:38:57,640
Can you not call it sulking?

490
00:38:58,280 --> 00:39:00,000
It makes me sound like a kid.

491
00:39:02,120 --> 00:39:04,320
I really am sorry about Grandpa.

492
00:39:05,640 --> 00:39:07,920
I honestly wasn't trying
to get close to anyone.

493
00:39:08,880 --> 00:39:10,320
You don't need to worry.

494
00:39:11,120 --> 00:39:13,760
I just want to do my job as well as I can.
That's all.

495
00:39:14,960 --> 00:39:18,200
I know. I was overthinking it.

496
00:39:20,760 --> 00:39:22,920
And about renting Mr. Nimit's house,

497
00:39:23,000 --> 00:39:24,840
-I just wanted to--
-I'm jealous.

498
00:39:28,080 --> 00:39:29,720
I know I have no right to be.

499
00:39:31,120 --> 00:39:33,080
Alyssa and I aren't together.

500
00:39:34,440 --> 00:39:36,040
I love her, but it's one-sided.

501
00:39:39,560 --> 00:39:41,240
You don't need to worry about me.

502
00:39:42,040 --> 00:39:44,040
I really don't have feelings
for Ms. Alyssa.

503
00:39:44,760 --> 00:39:46,080
Really, Wee?

504
00:39:46,160 --> 00:39:47,280
Really.

505
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:50,280
So you're not mad at me anymore?

506
00:39:50,360 --> 00:39:52,000
Let's take Mom out for a meal.

507
00:39:53,000 --> 00:39:54,880
We're all here together.

508
00:39:56,480 --> 00:39:58,560
I don't think today's a good idea.

509
00:40:01,040 --> 00:40:04,560
I feel like Ms. Pimpa is watching us.

510
00:40:06,760 --> 00:40:08,400
Okay, that's fine.

511
00:40:09,280 --> 00:40:13,240
Next time, then.
Mom's in Bangkok for a few more days.

512
00:40:36,560 --> 00:40:37,960
Korn.

513
00:40:39,880 --> 00:40:40,960
Hello, Uncle.

514
00:40:41,720 --> 00:40:42,800
Hi.

515
00:40:43,920 --> 00:40:44,880
Want to grab a bite?

516
00:41:02,000 --> 00:41:06,120
Hey, don't be so nervous. Relax.

517
00:41:11,040 --> 00:41:13,800
I'd like us to get to know each other.

518
00:41:15,440 --> 00:41:16,800
Bring your glass over.

519
00:41:21,360 --> 00:41:22,640
Thank you.

520
00:41:29,280 --> 00:41:30,760
You don't need to be afraid of me.

521
00:41:31,680 --> 00:41:33,480
I'm nothing like your Aunt Pim.

522
00:41:33,560 --> 00:41:36,160
And I've got nothing against your mother.

523
00:41:36,240 --> 00:41:38,520
I think of Da as my own sister.

524
00:41:39,840 --> 00:41:41,200
Well…

525
00:41:41,280 --> 00:41:43,800
I'm not after the inheritance
like Aunt Pim, either.

526
00:41:45,960 --> 00:41:49,000
I'm better off not wanting any of it.

527
00:41:50,280 --> 00:41:53,600
I've got enough money
to last a lifetime. Right?

528
00:41:57,360 --> 00:41:58,480
I guess so.

529
00:41:59,040 --> 00:42:01,840
But Aunt Pim doesn't like me

530
00:42:01,920 --> 00:42:04,040
because I'm Mom's son, does she?

531
00:42:06,280 --> 00:42:07,240
That's part of it.

532
00:42:08,440 --> 00:42:10,920
You're also the only grandson
in the Tayawat family.

533
00:42:11,720 --> 00:42:12,920
That worries her.

534
00:42:15,120 --> 00:42:17,960
Doesn't Aunt Pim have a family of her own?

535
00:42:19,920 --> 00:42:21,160
She did.

536
00:42:21,920 --> 00:42:23,520
A husband and a son.

537
00:42:24,440 --> 00:42:26,840
Her son died when he was little.

538
00:42:27,720 --> 00:42:29,000
Then her marriage fell apart.

539
00:42:30,160 --> 00:42:32,520
Her husband couldn't put up
with her nonsense.

540
00:42:33,560 --> 00:42:37,680
He found another woman.
They divorced years ago.

541
00:42:40,720 --> 00:42:42,280
I feel sorry for her.

542
00:42:44,440 --> 00:42:46,120
She brought it all on herself.

543
00:42:47,680 --> 00:42:51,160
What about you? Don't you want a family?

544
00:42:51,240 --> 00:42:54,520
Hey, are you interviewing me now?

545
00:42:55,480 --> 00:42:56,480
Can I?

546
00:42:58,080 --> 00:43:01,480
Sure, nephew. Bring your glass over.

547
00:43:03,520 --> 00:43:04,680
You know what?

548
00:43:05,520 --> 00:43:09,000
I like being single too much.

549
00:43:09,920 --> 00:43:10,960
I hate being told what to do.

550
00:43:11,720 --> 00:43:13,200
I keep things casual with women

551
00:43:14,080 --> 00:43:15,600
and trade stocks day by day.

552
00:43:16,760 --> 00:43:18,160
Life's pretty damn good.

553
00:43:18,240 --> 00:43:19,560
You trade stocks?

554
00:43:20,440 --> 00:43:21,480
Yeah.

555
00:43:24,760 --> 00:43:26,120
My portfolio's looking good.

556
00:43:26,760 --> 00:43:28,200
I hate to brag.

557
00:43:29,040 --> 00:43:29,880
Wow.

558
00:43:39,280 --> 00:43:44,520
Nada Tayawat attacked…

559
00:43:50,680 --> 00:43:53,840
TAYAWAT FOUNDATION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN,
A LOOK INSIDE THE TAYAWAT FAMILY MANSION

560
00:43:53,920 --> 00:43:57,640
NADA TAYAWAT'S SIX-MONTH-OLD SON VANISHED
DURING A FAMILY TRIP TO TAWAN ISLAND

561
00:43:57,720 --> 00:44:02,560
THE UNSOLVED DISAPPEARANCE
OF NADA TAYAWAT'S SIX-MONTH-OLD SON

562
00:44:07,400 --> 00:44:09,920
IN OCTOBER 1999, THE COUPLE
WERE VACATIONING ON TAWAN ISLAND

563
00:44:14,280 --> 00:44:15,720
October…

564
00:44:15,800 --> 00:44:19,720
WHEN THEIR SIX-MONTH-OLD SON WENT MISSING
NO LEADS HAVE BEEN FOUND SO FAR

565
00:44:26,320 --> 00:44:31,600
"They believe it happened while the two
were vacationing on Tawan Island."

566
00:44:33,800 --> 00:44:35,960
Tawan Island?

567
00:44:36,840 --> 00:44:38,960
Why has Dad never told me about this?

568
00:44:40,800 --> 00:44:42,800
I need the DNA test results.

569
00:44:43,440 --> 00:44:44,640
Please help me.

570
00:44:44,720 --> 00:44:47,280
For Ms. Nada and Mr. Phakorn?

571
00:44:48,000 --> 00:44:49,800
Rawee's too.

572
00:44:55,720 --> 00:44:57,320
But the child died.

573
00:44:58,520 --> 00:45:00,440
Did they pass Phakorn off as him?

574
00:45:03,640 --> 00:45:05,640
Then why test Mr. Rawee's DNA?

575
00:45:12,480 --> 00:45:13,840
Thank you.

576
00:45:16,720 --> 00:45:19,760
It was nice of Mr. Panas
to send someone to pick me up.

577
00:45:19,840 --> 00:45:22,360
That family's kind too, actually.

578
00:45:22,440 --> 00:45:24,280
He sent someone to get you?

579
00:45:25,600 --> 00:45:28,240
Yes. He said it was on Phakorn's behalf.

580
00:45:28,320 --> 00:45:30,400
I even got to visit Ms. Nada.

581
00:45:33,920 --> 00:45:35,600
I got to see Korn too.

582
00:45:36,280 --> 00:45:39,360
He must have known I was worried.

583
00:45:39,440 --> 00:45:41,000
But it's strange.

584
00:45:41,080 --> 00:45:42,880
Korn told me

585
00:45:42,960 --> 00:45:46,200
his aunt hasn't been very kind to him.

586
00:45:47,400 --> 00:45:48,680
Ms. Pimpa?

587
00:45:49,400 --> 00:45:51,400
Yes, that's her.

588
00:45:52,080 --> 00:45:53,760
He said she doesn't accept him

589
00:45:53,840 --> 00:45:56,320
and is always picking on him.

590
00:45:59,200 --> 00:46:01,600
I still find it strange that Mr. Panas

591
00:46:01,680 --> 00:46:03,320
sent someone to pick you up.

592
00:46:07,560 --> 00:46:09,040
Maybe he's kind to us

593
00:46:09,120 --> 00:46:11,680
because we raised Korn.

594
00:46:12,760 --> 00:46:14,000
Oh, Wee.

595
00:46:14,080 --> 00:46:16,520
Have you said hello to Alyssa?

596
00:46:16,600 --> 00:46:19,880
Mr. Nimit said she lives across from you.

597
00:46:19,960 --> 00:46:22,120
I've seen her a few times.

598
00:46:22,200 --> 00:46:25,000
Mom, Ms. Alyssa's seeing Korn.

599
00:46:28,240 --> 00:46:29,600
Really, Wee?

600
00:46:29,680 --> 00:46:31,960
Korn hasn't told me anything.

601
00:46:36,920 --> 00:46:38,600
Are you okay with that?

602
00:46:40,160 --> 00:46:41,600
Okay with what, Mom?

603
00:46:43,280 --> 00:46:45,480
With Korn seeing Alyssa.

604
00:46:47,640 --> 00:46:49,040
Of course I am.

605
00:46:49,560 --> 00:46:51,320
Korn's grown up.

606
00:46:52,080 --> 00:46:55,160
He can decide who he wants to see.

607
00:46:59,520 --> 00:47:00,440
Mom!

608
00:47:01,240 --> 00:47:03,200
I don't have feelings for Ms. Alyssa.

609
00:47:03,880 --> 00:47:05,160
Okay, as long as you're okay.

610
00:47:05,840 --> 00:47:07,440
I'll ask Korn about it later.

611
00:47:08,400 --> 00:47:09,840
Are you going

612
00:47:09,920 --> 00:47:11,880
to visit Ms. Nada tomorrow?

613
00:47:27,120 --> 00:47:29,640
And about renting Mr. Nimit's house,

614
00:47:29,720 --> 00:47:31,640
-I just wanted to--
-I'm jealous.

615
00:47:34,840 --> 00:47:36,440
I know I have no right to be.

616
00:47:37,560 --> 00:47:39,640
Alyssa and I aren't together.

617
00:47:41,080 --> 00:47:42,840
I love her, but it's one-sided.

618
00:47:46,080 --> 00:47:47,840
You don't need to worry about me.

619
00:47:48,680 --> 00:47:50,680
I really don't have feelings
for Ms. Alyssa.

620
00:47:51,360 --> 00:47:52,720
Really, Wee?

621
00:47:52,800 --> 00:47:54,040
Really.

622
00:47:54,600 --> 00:47:56,920
So you're not mad at me anymore?

623
00:48:15,080 --> 00:48:17,320
So, Uncle, do you think

624
00:48:17,400 --> 00:48:19,080
I could trade stocks too?

625
00:48:20,680 --> 00:48:22,040
Of course.

626
00:48:22,120 --> 00:48:23,040
Easy.

627
00:48:23,120 --> 00:48:25,720
It's in our family's DNA.

628
00:48:25,800 --> 00:48:28,360
Next time I see you at the office,

629
00:48:28,440 --> 00:48:30,080
I'll help you open a trading account.

630
00:48:30,160 --> 00:48:34,520
Or you can try trading with mine first.

631
00:48:34,600 --> 00:48:38,840
It's okay, Uncle. I'd rather open my own.
I don't want to impose.

632
00:48:40,360 --> 00:48:43,200
Don't worry about that.
It'd be good for me too.

633
00:48:43,280 --> 00:48:45,200
I'd have someone to talk stocks with.

634
00:48:45,720 --> 00:48:49,280
The women I talk to don't really get it.

635
00:48:52,440 --> 00:48:53,480
Thank you, Uncle.

636
00:48:54,120 --> 00:48:55,200
Hey.

637
00:48:56,680 --> 00:48:57,520
Remember this, Korn.

638
00:48:58,600 --> 00:49:01,040
Don't just rely on the Tayawat money.

639
00:49:01,760 --> 00:49:03,760
It's best to earn your own money.

640
00:49:04,720 --> 00:49:06,200
That's real freedom.

641
00:49:13,440 --> 00:49:17,880
"THE HEART OF SUCCESS IS HAPPINESS"
NADA TAYAWAT

642
00:49:39,560 --> 00:49:41,240
<i>Every time I see Father,</i>

643
00:49:41,320 --> 00:49:43,600
<i>he asks me to work at the company.</i>

644
00:49:44,360 --> 00:49:46,240
<i>I've told him so many times</i>
<i>I don't want to.</i>

645
00:49:46,320 --> 00:49:49,320
<i>I just don't. I hate working at a company.</i>

646
00:49:55,640 --> 00:49:57,840
"I want a little cafe of my own,

647
00:49:57,920 --> 00:50:00,720
decorated just the way I like it."

648
00:50:19,360 --> 00:50:20,560
"Times change."

649
00:50:21,520 --> 00:50:22,720
"People change."

650
00:51:37,240 --> 00:51:39,960
-Hello, Aunt Pim.
-Oh, hello, Alyssa.

651
00:51:40,040 --> 00:51:41,320
Here to see Nada?

652
00:51:41,400 --> 00:51:42,840
Yes.

653
00:51:42,920 --> 00:51:44,680
Have you seen her already?

654
00:51:45,280 --> 00:51:49,000
Not yet. I thought
I'd have a coffee first, then go in.

655
00:52:08,360 --> 00:52:11,640
I need the DNA test results.
Please help me.

656
00:52:11,720 --> 00:52:14,560
For Ms. Nada and Mr. Phakorn?

657
00:52:15,160 --> 00:52:16,680
Rawee's too.

658
00:52:19,800 --> 00:52:22,200
I'll give you something for your trouble.

659
00:52:23,160 --> 00:52:25,440
For the risk you're taking.

660
00:52:27,320 --> 00:52:28,520
Please help me.

661
00:52:45,120 --> 00:52:48,320
-Is she your friend, Aunt Pim?
-Oh, she's my junior.

662
00:52:49,760 --> 00:52:50,960
Shall we go?

663
00:52:52,520 --> 00:52:53,600
Come on.

664
00:53:13,160 --> 00:53:14,120
Hello, Wee.

665
00:53:14,720 --> 00:53:17,320
You don't need to come
to the hospital today.

666
00:53:17,400 --> 00:53:19,880
I've moved Mom to another room.

667
00:53:19,960 --> 00:53:22,360
Please let Taddao know too.

668
00:53:23,160 --> 00:53:26,720
You can take care of things at work.
I'll look after Mom.

669
00:53:35,760 --> 00:53:37,080
Oh, sorry.

670
00:53:40,360 --> 00:53:43,120
It's work. I need to take this call.

671
00:53:43,920 --> 00:53:47,000
Alright. You know which room, right?

672
00:53:47,840 --> 00:53:48,800
Yes.

673
00:53:50,240 --> 00:53:51,480
Hello?

674
00:53:56,680 --> 00:53:57,800
Okay.

675
00:54:00,320 --> 00:54:03,960
Yes, let's do that. Thank you.

676
00:54:06,720 --> 00:54:08,000
Oh, sorry.

677
00:54:09,440 --> 00:54:11,600
Are those documents for Aunt Pim?

678
00:54:11,680 --> 00:54:12,840
Yes.

679
00:54:14,600 --> 00:54:17,200
She's in the middle
of a serious conversation.

680
00:54:18,120 --> 00:54:19,800
You can leave them with me for now.

681
00:54:19,880 --> 00:54:22,560
-Well…
-I know

682
00:54:22,640 --> 00:54:24,920
they're very important.

683
00:54:25,640 --> 00:54:28,000
I'll hand them to her myself.

684
00:54:42,200 --> 00:54:44,440
Please make sure she gets them.

685
00:54:45,600 --> 00:54:46,920
Of course.

686
00:55:15,480 --> 00:55:17,160
Look at you.

687
00:55:29,040 --> 00:55:29,880
Hello?

688
00:55:30,840 --> 00:55:32,720
The DNA results are in?

689
00:55:33,640 --> 00:55:35,640
Is Phakorn Nada's son?

690
00:55:38,160 --> 00:55:41,160
He isn't? No match at all?

691
00:55:43,160 --> 00:55:44,200
Are you sure?

692
00:55:44,800 --> 00:55:46,880
What about Rawee?

693
00:55:46,960 --> 00:55:49,280
Does his DNA match Nada's?

694
00:55:51,520 --> 00:55:52,920
No?

695
00:55:55,880 --> 00:55:57,120
I see.

696
00:55:59,040 --> 00:56:00,920
Where are the results now?

697
00:56:04,280 --> 00:56:05,360
You left them with…?

698
00:56:06,000 --> 00:56:09,760
Oh, okay. I'll come get them right away.

699
00:56:10,400 --> 00:56:11,720
Bye.

700
00:56:22,280 --> 00:56:24,400
Mother and son both put on quite an act.

701
00:56:25,760 --> 00:56:27,880
Just you wait. This time,

702
00:56:28,520 --> 00:56:31,240
I'll bring you down, Nada.

703
00:56:53,880 --> 00:56:55,840
A nurse asked me to give you this.

704
00:57:33,400 --> 00:57:35,120
Who gave you your name?

705
00:57:35,720 --> 00:57:38,640
-My mother, Sir.
-The names sound so alike.

706
00:57:38,720 --> 00:57:39,720
<i>Aunt Da</i>

707
00:57:40,320 --> 00:57:42,600
left Korn in your care when he was little?

708
00:57:43,640 --> 00:57:45,960
Yes, since he was a baby.

709
00:57:46,880 --> 00:57:47,920
How many months old?

710
00:57:50,200 --> 00:57:51,840
<i>What are you suspecting?</i>

711
00:57:52,760 --> 00:57:54,080
<i>Do you think</i>

712
00:57:54,160 --> 00:57:56,960
Korn is pretending to be Ms. Nada's son?

713
00:57:58,960 --> 00:58:02,400
Wee, if we tell everyone
the whole truth now,

714
00:58:02,480 --> 00:58:04,520
<i>will it be too late?</i>

715
00:58:06,080 --> 00:58:08,000
<i>This isn't something</i>
<i>to take lightly, Korn.</i>

716
00:58:10,760 --> 00:58:12,720
<i>We don't know what might happen.</i>

717
00:58:14,880 --> 00:58:17,400
<i>You're her real son.</i>

718
00:58:17,480 --> 00:58:18,920
<i>If anything happens to me,</i>

719
00:58:19,000 --> 00:58:19,920
<i>you have to help me.</i>

720
00:58:58,320 --> 00:59:00,440
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
